 "headline": {
  "en": "ALERT: The rains reached Garissa on the night of Thursday 12 November. 6 mm fell on Garissa in the last 3 days (30 mm on 13 Nov). The River Tana is rising – flow is 4.3× its dry early-October level. Indicative Garissa gauge ~4.36 m now, ~4.41 m by 26 Nov (wettest run 5.25 m).",
  "sw": "ALERT: Mvua zilifika Garissa usiku wa Alhamisi 12 Novemba. Mvua ya mm 6 imenyesha Garissa siku 3 zilizopita. Mto Tana unazidi kupanda – kiwango cha kipimo cha Garissa kinakadiriwa mita 4.36 sasa na mita 4.41 kufikia 26 Nov.",
  "so": "ALERT: Roobabku waxay gaareen Garissa habeenkii Khamiista 12 Nofeembar. 6 mm roob ah ayaa ka da'ay Garissa 3dii maalmood ee la soo dhaafay. Webiga Tana wuu sii kacayaa – cabbirka Garissa qiyaastii 4.36 m hadda, 4.41 m ilaa 26 Nov."
 },
 "actions": [
  "Riverine farmers: move pumps, generators and livestock off the floodplain now – do not wait for the river to reach 4 m.",
  "Do not walk or drive through flowing laghas or flooded roads.",
  "Boil or treat drinking water; clear stagnant water around homes (malaria, cholera).",
  "Report flooding, trapped people or damaged roads: Kenya Red Cross 1199 or emergency@garissa.go.ke."
